<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Greco-Bactrian Kingdom</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Greco-Bactrian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Greco-Bactrian Kingdom was a Hellenistic state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bactria">Bactria</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, founded when Greek governors broke away from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> in the third century BCE. It became a meeting point of Greek, Iranian and Indian cultures. Its secession illustrates the fragmentation of the Seleucid Empire's eastern provinces and the spread of Greek culture far into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/greco-bactrian-kingdom.jpg" alt="Greco-Bactrian Kingdom" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. World Imaging assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greco-BactrianKingdomMap.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
